WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Welcome to our training on how to respond to an Amazon Anti-Counterfeiting Policy Violation.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.429
The tips we'll share in this video don't take the place of legal advice, so remember to consult

00:00:12.429 --> 00:00:16.000
a lawyer if you have any specific anti-counterfeiting questions.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:22.632
When you list products in the Amazon store, you'll need to comply with all applicable laws and Amazon

00:00:22.632 --> 00:00:23.000
policies.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:28.760
One of these policies is the Amazon Anti-Counterfeiting Policy, which helps ensure that all products

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:32.000
offered for sale in the Amazon store are authentic.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:38.737
If we believe your account has violated the Amazon Anti-Counterfeiting Policy, we'll send you an

00:00:38.737 --> 00:00:40.000
authenticity-related violation.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:46.737
To review this and other performance notifications, select the menu icon in the top-left corner

00:00:46.737 --> 00:00:48.000
of Seller Central.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.000
Hover over Performance and select Performance Notifications.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:56.000
You can also review performance information on your account health page.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:02.533
To get there, hover over Performance, select Account Health, and click Product Authenticity Customer

00:01:02.533 --> 00:01:03.000
Complaints.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:09.000
If we notify you of a violation, you should correct the behavior described in the notification.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:15.222
If you don't believe that you violated the Anti-Counterfeiting Policy, submit an appeal as soon

00:01:15.222 --> 00:01:16.000
as possible.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:22.095
When you submit an appeal for an anti-counterfeiting policy violation, you'll need to submit copies

00:01:22.095 --> 00:01:24.000
of invoices from your suppliers.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:29.000
We'll use the documents you provide to verify the authenticity of your products.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:37.095
These invoices must include a clearly displayed issue date within the past 365 days and before you

00:01:37.095 --> 00:01:39.000
received the performance notification.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:47.143
Your sales volume for each ASIN over the past 365 days, each of the requested ASINs with all highlighted

00:01:47.143 --> 00:01:48.000
for clarity,

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:54.000
and the contact information of your supplier, including a name, phone number, address, and website.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:59.000
We won't share this information with our retail team or other Amazon sellers.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:03.000
Any documents you provide must be authentic and unaltered.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:08.000
In other words, we won't be able to accept invoices that have been digitally manipulated.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:14.737
You can remove pricing information from the invoices, but make sure that all other information is

00:02:14.737 --> 00:02:16.000
visible and clear.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:20.000
Once you've gathered your invoices, return to the account health page.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:26.000
Select Product Authenticity Customer Complaints and click "Appeal" next to the policy violation.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:32.136
Here, you'll submit the requested documents by clicking the "Select Files" button or dragging and

00:02:32.136 --> 00:02:35.000
dropping the files into the available field.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:41.588
Select the checkboxes next to each requirement to confirm your documents meet them and then click "

00:02:41.588 --> 00:02:42.000
Submit."

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:46.000
Once you've submitted the appeal, we'll review your provided documents.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:52.800
We might reach out to the supplier to verify your document's information and will always keep your

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:54.000
supplier's information confidential.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:57.000
If your appeal is approved, we'll reinstate your listing.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:04.000
To review the Amazon Anti-Counterfeiting Policy, search "Anti-Counterfeiting Policy" in Seller Central.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:10.000
This concludes our training on how to respond to an Amazon Anti-Counterfeiting Policy violation.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:14.000
Thank you and happy selling in the Amazon Store!
